WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:18.381
the shop Scrooge could see that Wilkins' face had more wrinkles now.

2
00:00:19.742 --> 00:00:23.723
But Wilkins' smile looked brighter than ever as he spoke to a young boy.

3
00:00:23.743 --> 00:00:27.324
"Tell me, Edward," Wilkins said.

4
00:00:28.404 --> 00:00:33.568
"Have you been outside, looking at all the Christmas decorations in the neighborhood?"

5
00:00:33.588 --> 00:00:38.131
"Yes, Grandfather," the boy said eagerly.

6
00:00:38.151 --> 00:00:42.534
"I love all of them—especially the wreaths and garlands.

7
00:00:43.654 --> 00:00:45.095
It's sunny out, but guess what!

8
00:00:45.436 --> 00:00:48.138
It's so cold that the lake in the park is frozen.

9
00:00:48.158 --> 00:00:54.042
I heard people saying they've never seen such a perfect day for ice skating."

10
00:00:54.062 --> 00:00:59.493
"Hmm." Wilkins chuckled.

11
00:00:59.513 --> 00:01:03.497
"It sounds like someone might like to go skating today.

12
00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:09.122
Maybe I can close the shop early, and we can go before dinner.

13
00:01:10.022 --> 00:01:11.344
How does that sound?"

14
00:01:11.364 --> 00:01:14.446
"Really?" Edward said.

15
00:01:14.466 --> 00:01:16.728
"We can go skating?"

16
00:01:16.748 --> 00:01:21.032
"Of course," Wilkins said.

17
00:01:21.052 --> 00:01:28.661
"When I opened this shop, I promised myself that I would never let work become more important than

18
00:01:28.881 --> 00:01:33.402
family. And do you know who taught me this valuable lesson?

19
00:01:33.422 --> 00:01:36.183
"Who, Grandfather?"

20
00:01:36.643 --> 00:01:37.363
Edward asked.

21
00:01:37.383 --> 00:01:44.085
"A very wealthy businessman named Ebenezer Scrooge," Wilkins said.

22
00:01:44.105 --> 00:01:51.327
"He actually taught me many important things about work."

23
00:01:51.347 --> 00:01:52.467
Scrooge gasped.

24
00:01:52.487 --> 00:01:55.048
"This is wonderful, spirit!

25
00:01:56.204 --> 00:01:59.868
Good old Dick Wilkins sounds as if he is quite fond of me.

26
00:02:01.389 --> 00:02:04.512
He always did look up to me when we worked together."

27
00:02:07.115 --> 00:02:10.158
Wilkins reached for a newspaper that was lying on the table.

28
00:02:11.159 --> 00:02:13.201
He opened it to a page with obituaries.

29
00:02:13.221 --> 00:02:16.644
"See this notice, Edward?

30
00:02:18.386 --> 00:02:20.468
Mr. Scrooge died recently.

31
00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:26.684
But he was survived by no family, except for one nephew.

32
00:02:27.925 --> 00:02:31.568
And from what I hear, he had no friends at all."

33
00:02:32.769 --> 00:02:33.890
Wilkins shook his head.

34
00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:36.332
"It's a shame.

35
00:02:37.212 --> 00:02:41.956
I knew him long ago, and he was a nice enough fellow back then."

36
00:02:41.976 --> 00:02:45.659
"Were the two of you once friends then?"

37
00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:47.341
Edward asked curiously.

38
00:02:47.361 --> 00:02:51.244
"Well, I tried my best to be his friend."

39
00:02:52.296 --> 00:02:54.938
Wilkins folded the newspaper, setting it aside.

40
00:02:54.958 --> 00:02:58.481
"We worked together for a year or two.

41
00:02:59.621 --> 00:03:05.085
After that, he started a new business with a clever businessman named Marley.

42
00:03:06.506 --> 00:03:14.072
At the time Ebenezer was courting a lovely young woman named Belle who seemed to make him happy.

43
00:03:15.313 --> 00:03:22.518
But with every passing month, Ebenezer spent more time working and less time doing anything else.

44
00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:29.725
I went to visit him a few times, but he had no time for me or anyone else.

45
00:03:31.367 --> 00:03:33.949
He was too busy thinking about money."

46
00:03:36.712 --> 00:03:37.933
Wilkins shook his head.

47
00:03:39.134 --> 00:03:45.480
"Remember this, Edward: A relationship that's neglected will wither and die."

48
00:03:48.668 --> 00:03:50.029
Wilkins suddenly stood up.

49
00:03:50.049 --> 00:03:54.573
"But never mind all that; it's ancient history now.

50
00:03:55.814 --> 00:04:01.459
I'll finish up a couple of things at the shop, and then we can go skating."

51
00:04:03.541 --> 00:04:08.685
Before Scrooge could say anything, the scene faded, and was quickly replaced by another.

52
00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:13.069
He and the ghost now stood in a warm sitting room.

53
00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:19.382
Flower petals were strewn on the floor, and white fabric was draped over furniture.

54
00:04:20.922 --> 00:04:23.764
Belle was there, her hair now touched with gray.

55
00:04:24.805 --> 00:04:28.427
She was beaming at a beautiful young woman wearing a wedding dress.

56
00:04:30.348 --> 00:04:33.350
Belle adjusted one of the sleeves on the young woman's dress.

57
00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:36.392
"There, that looks perfect.

58
00:04:37.412 --> 00:04:41.174
I can hardly believe it—my youngest child is getting married!"

59
00:04:42.395 --> 00:04:43.436
Her daughter hugged her.

60
00:04:44.456 --> 00:04:46.937
"I'm excited but also very nervous."

61
00:04:46.957 --> 00:04:50.399
"I understand."

62
00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.120
Belle smiled.

63
00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:54.181
"I was nervous too.

64
00:04:55.362 --> 00:04:59.204
But just remember how happy your father has made me all these years.

65
00:05:00.665 --> 00:05:02.606
I can't imagine my life without him."

66
00:05:02.626 --> 00:05:07.369
"You were older than I am when you married him," the daughter said.

67
00:05:07.389 --> 00:05:11.451
"Other men must have courted you before you met Papa."

68
00:05:12.551 --> 00:05:13.372
Belle shrugged.

69
00:05:14.244 --> 00:05:15.524
"I suppose they did."

70
00:05:16.445 --> 00:05:18.725
She tilted her head with a thoughtful expression.

71
00:05:18.745 --> 00:05:22.726
"In fact, I nearly got married once before."

72
00:05:22.746 --> 00:05:26.528
"What?" Her daughter looked shocked.

73
00:05:26.548 --> 00:05:28.868
"Why, I never knew that!

74
00:05:29.848 --> 00:05:31.549
Who was the man you almost married?"

75
00:05:31.569 --> 00:05:36.070
"His name was Ebenezer Scrooge," Belle said.

76
00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:42.112
"I loved him, but I realized in the nick of time that he loved something else more."

77
00:05:44.512 --> 00:05:47.493
"Oh!" The daughter peered closely at Belle.

78
00:05:49.013 --> 00:05:50.954
"He fell in love with another woman?"

79
00:05:52.674 --> 00:05:53.455
Belle laughed.

80
00:05:53.475 --> 00:05:58.116
"No, he fell in love with money, and only that.

81
00:05:59.336 --> 00:06:03.177
And then, thank goodness, I later met my true love, your papa."

82
00:06:04.878 --> 00:06:07.739
Scrooge felt a sharp jolt at Belle's words.

83
00:06:08.619 --> 00:06:16.340
Then Dick Wilkins' words floated through his mind too: "A relationship that is neglected will wither and die."

84
00:06:18.622 --> 00:06:20.684
Scrooge clutched his head in pain.

85
00:06:20.704 --> 00:06:24.027
"What have I done to myself?"

86
00:06:24.647 --> 00:06:25.148
he thought.

87
00:06:26.389 --> 00:06:27.430
He knew the answer.

88
00:06:28.911 --> 00:06:33.135
He had allowed the most precious things in his life to wither and die.
